# Eval case: public_network
#
# ablate.patch removes latitudesh_public_network — resource and data source: Go
# files, tests, registration, manifest entry, lock rows, templates, example and
# rendered docs — so the PublicNetworks SDK group reappears in the pending queue.
# Its derived shape is CR-D -> resource + datasource, exactly what the repo ships,
# so KINDS is not pinned.
#
# Why this case: the merged resource is the reference implementation for the
# prompt-v7 rules that closed the three P1 findings on PR #250 — a configured
# `project` slug preserved instead of overwritten by the API's ID, slug->ID
# resolution before the POST, a reconciling GET after create, an import that
# fills every Required/RequiresReplace input, and a not-found helper that
# recognises both SDK error shapes. A regression on any of them shows up as a
# diff against the known-good files (run with --keep and compare the worktree to
# HEAD) — the gate itself only scores well-formedness. The elastic_ip case cannot
# exercise these: it predates all of them.
#
# By design this case also removes the prompt's PRIMARY exemplar for exactly
# those rules (resource_public_network.go). The agent therefore works from the
# rules' own wording plus the secondary exemplars the prompt names for each
# pattern (marketplaceAppNotFound, resource_virtual_machine_backup.go's Create,
# resource_elastic_ip.go's effectiveProject, the IsNull()||IsUnknown() guards in
# resource_elastic_ip_bgp.go and resource_virtual_network.go) — which is the
# situation a genuinely new group is in. A run that only passes when the
# reference file is present would not be measuring the prompt.
GROUP=PublicNetworks
DESCRIPTION="CR-D resource + data source; exercises selector preservation, import completeness, reconciling create, and both SDK error shapes."
